solutions.latex:
\exfigure{515_q24_s1}

Three applications of the trapezoidal rule on $0\le t\le3$ give $h=\dfrac{3-0}{3}=1$, with $y=V$ read from the graph at $t=0,1,2,3$: $y_0=10,\ y_1=3.68,\ y_2=2.43,\ y_3=1.77$.
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Volume} &\approx \dfrac{h}{2}\left[y_0+y_3+2(y_1+y_2)\right] \\ &= \dfrac{1}{2}\left[10+1.77+2(3.68+2.43)\right] \\ &= 11.995\ \text{units}^3 \end{aligned}$$

